# Hooks Disabled

All bash-based hooks have been removed.

Reason: Windows PowerShell incompatibility + more overhead than savings.
Token optimization is now purely behavioral (see .kimi/rules/token-optimization.md).

Previous hooks:
- post-write-hook.sh — credential scanning + file validation
- pre-command-hook.sh — package management security check
- pre-commit-hook.sh — git commit credential exposure check
- session-end-hook.sh — session summary + cleanup

These are preserved in git history if needed for reference.
